      en: "Khor al-Subiya is a large bay in northwestern Kuwait, shaped by the ancient Euphrates delta. It extends about 30 km along the Persian Gulf coast and features extensive tidal flats and salt marshes. The bay is a critical stopover for migratory birds, with over 100 species recorded, including greater flamingos and terns. Geologically, it consists of Holocene sediments deposited by river and marine processes. The archaeological site of Subiya reveals Ubaid-period settlements (c. 5000 BCE). Economically, the area supports fishing and shrimp farming. Environmental concerns include oil pollution and habitat degradation.",
